# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Accounts — Clerk
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# On Vercel: `vercel integration add clerk --plan hobby_2025_08`, or
# Dashboard -> Integrations -> Clerk. Both vars are injected automatically.
#
# Locally, run `npx vercel env pull .env.local` after installing.
#
# CLERK_SECRET_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Database — you should NOT need to fill these in by hand.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# On Vercel: Project Dashboard -> Storage -> Create Database -> Upstash for Redis
# -> connect it to this project. The vars below are injected automatically.
#
# Locally, run `npx vercel env pull .env.local` after linking the store.
#
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_URL=
# UPSTASH_REDIS_REST_TOKEN=
#
# Legacy Vercel KV stores are also supported via:
# KV_REST_API_URL=
# KV_REST_API_TOKEN=
